Z||000001||Wade87GT||06-26-2001||10:47 PM||||Try swapping out your 2.8 for a Quad 4. Of course, you'll have to port, polish, balance, and blueprint it. Do it right and you might get that motor to sing at 9,000 RPM. Don't forget to add a turbo, NOX, high flow cat and free flow big bore exhaust system. After all that you probably won't need the "coffee can" tip.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Wade87GT (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||mrgone||06-26-2001||10:51 PM||||check out the muffler that those rice rockets are sportin   the big chrome ones that are right at the tip. one of those may do it for you.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroPerformance||06-27-2001||12:16 AM||||STOP! Before you do anything have someone else drive your car and follow it around. The V6 sounds so good I freak out every time I get a chance to hear mine running from outside of the car. If you still are hooked on the "rice" sound then look into resonating exhaust tips. Personaly I think the hondas sound good for about 30 seconds and then it gives me a headache. I wouldn't trade mine for theirs I can tell you that much.<P>-Charlie<p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||06-27-2001||09:16 AM||||Replace your cat with a Cherry bomb, see how it sounds... then replace muffler with West Coast's Flowmaster     that should give you a completely different exaust sound<BR>or else for rice stuff: <A HREF="http://www.acautotechnic.com" TARGET=_blank>www.acautotechnic.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.stylincompacts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.stylincompacts.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.4apc.com" TARGET=_blank>www.4apc.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.contemporarymotorsport.com/sst" TARGET=_blank>www.contemporarymotorsport.com/sst</A>  <A HREF="http://www.magnaflow.com" TARGET=_blank>www.magnaflow.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.shmotorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shmotorsport.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.autobahnwholesale.com" TARGET=_blank>www.autobahnwholesale.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A> <BR>that should be enough (looking thorough super steet mag)||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||06-27-2001||09:36 AM||||Yeah, cherry bombs.  I had a couple of 16" bombs behind a big block 390.  They didn't quiet much, but they gave it that snap, crackle, and pop "hot rod" sound.  Enough to have a cop follow me almost every day to see what I was up to. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  You have to dot your I's and cross your T's in a small town with exhaust like that. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">(at least around the law)||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||06-27-2001||02:57 PM||||real ricer sound?<P>drop in a duke, straight pipes with no muffler, and put a 4" exhaust tip on it.. and then run it at 4000 RPM all the time....<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Greg Piet||06-27-2001||03:00 PM||||Supertrapp??||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||06-27-2001||04:08 PM||||straight pipes and Pace Setter or Monza/Ansa resonated tips..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||06-27-2001||05:07 PM||||ya, exactly what darklord said. plus get lots of speed equipment decals, even if you dont have any of the parts.||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroHarry||06-27-2001||05:31 PM||||Take the cat out completely, then burn a hole in the muffler casing.<BR>Put really big coffee cans on it and dont forget the spare injectors and spark plugs routed to them for the big flame thrower effect. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Talk about an attention getter.......<P>(Just teasing dude)<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 266K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||14
Z||000011||Cozmo||06-27-2001||06:18 PM||||Bees.<BR>Put lots of bees in your trunk.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||10
Z||000012||firstfiero||06-27-2001||06:37 PM||||    Let me get this straight one of the top things about a fiero is the beautiful sound the v6 makes...and you want it to sound like a 4 cylinder thats trying to be a v6. Kids today!! damn...now I sound like my parents!<BR> <BR>very funny cozmo...but absolutly correct!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000013||qwikgta||06-28-2001||10:26 PM||||Before you get what you wish for, I just put a header on my DUKE.  I had no choice but to put a straight pipe on it (no room for a cat) and a Monza tip on the end.  IT IS WAY TO LOUD.... I just picked up a Supertrapp for it, I hope it tones it down some.  Trust me it sounds just like the rice when I shift at 5000.  <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||06-29-2001||12:18 AM||||I know... build a circuit with an MM5837 IC digital noise generator that produces the desired sound.. get a really quiet muffler, but put several subwoofers in your trunk. drive the amp with the circuit, and trigger it with a signal from the tach.. the higher the RPMs, the louder and higher pitched the sound from the subs.. could make your car sound like anything you wanted.. screaming F1 car.. rumbly 60s muscle car.. or an annoying, farting, buzzy ricer........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||6
Z||000015||Simple Fiero||06-29-2001||12:58 AM||||Look it is really easy, I did it all for 30 bucks Canadian, go to a auto store I went to CT. And look for RAPTOR exaust. No you won't be impressed right away but give it about 3 weeks and it will get loud trust me, and it is better than a cherry Bomb(there just crap) Screw spending hundreds on a flowmaster, or any of those others, the best part is that the raptor looks like a real exaust. Don't listen to these guys. You are 17 have fun be an annoying ass that is what you are to do, hell I am 25 and I am still doing it, LOL. You have to do what makes you happy, god american car drivers are way to patriot. Nothing is better than hearing the rumble of a 98 Skyline GTR with 1300hp. ||||reg||12
Z||000016||The Fieromaster||06-29-2001||01:07 PM||||I actually like some of the rice sounds.. like my buddys GT Probe when we cut the muffler off and ran a resonator tip.. Sounded like a honda on steroids.. you will never get that sound outta a Fiero cause exhaust is to short... you will get allot of the crackly rasp sound that normally is distorted by the long exhauset and the expasion cans!<BR>I like the 2.8 Fiero exhaust note anyway.. Some guyin a civic wanted to race cause my buddy yelled "this is a stock 4 wanna race" out my window... Well the dude wanted to race untill he heard my fly up on him... with my no "cat" having monster soundin v6! hehehe!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">    <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000017||Toddster||06-29-2001||01:20 PM||||Pull your GM engine and put in a donated engine from a sewing machine. Then attach a coffee can to the exhaust pipe and Viola! <P>Instant Rice!||||reg||1
Z||000018||GTMike||07-01-2001||05:03 AM||||i bet i know why you like that sound.  the movie fast and the feurious right. well i like the sound too.  but you realize they sound relly dumb at lower rpms.    but when they are screaming at 6 grand its kinda cool. why not keep the cat and go with out a muffler and make a y pipe or get a shop to make you one then put monza tips on your pipes.||||reg||1
